nodecode-octoprint is a rewrite of TakeshiTGAL's TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-print-job-watch:

  https://github.com/TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-print-job-watch
  commit 61cf86ed8c1a348c2d9956368e1abf7f51bb40fa
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TakeshiTGAL (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract. What the original
reaches is the same and it is reached the same way: one configured OctoPrint
origin, its /api/connection, /api/job and /api/printer readings, the
temperature block, the job file name, completion, file position and the
printTimeLeft estimate OctoPrint sends, POST /api/job with the same three
bodies (pause with action pause, pause with action resume, cancel), and one
optional webcam still that must sit on the printer's own host, JPEG or PNG,
under a byte cap, pruned to the newest 20. The watch diff is the original's:
printer_disconnected and error when the printer goes down, complete and
cancelled from the states the original names, paused only when a print was
running, and stalled when the file position, completion and file name all
stand still for stall_minutes; the per-print generation resets the reported
set, so an event is said once. A printer that cannot be reached is reported
once per cause, once a day after that, and once when it answers again, as the
original did. A state string is never taken as proof the printer moved; only
a later read is.

Left out, and why: Hermes's pre_tool_call approval hook, because Nodecode has
no approval prompt between the model and a tool -- the same guarantee is kept
inside the call instead, as a preview that sends nothing and a `confirm: true`
second call that reads the state, sends the move and reads it again. The cron
job, its generated script, the `schedule`/`unschedule` CLI verbs and the
delivery targets are replaced by a worker on `octoprint.watch_minutes` that
raises the same events as a standing notice while the cell runs; a notice is
not a chat message, so no delivery target is needed. The original's refusal to
follow a redirect that carries the API key is not re-implemented: the cell
sends the key to the configured origin only, and `snapshot_url` must be on the
printer's host, so a redirect away from it is the operator's own URL choice.
The plugin's skill is the manual topic `(help :octoprint)`, which every
request already carries a line of. The stills and the watch state live in
this cell's own folder under the Nodecode home, not in a plugin data
directory.

